_fg01.jpg/500px-Heupferd_fg01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Heupferd_fg01.jpg/500px-Heupferd_fg01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ensifera, like this great green bush-cricket Tettigonia viridissima, somewhat resemble grasshoppers but have over 20 segments in their antennae and different ovipositors.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHeupferd_fg01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Anacridium_aegyptium_-_01.jpg/500px-Anacridium_aegyptium_-_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Anacridium_aegyptium_-_01.jpg/1280px-Anacridium_aegyptium_-_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Anacridium_aegyptium_-_01.jpg/500px-Anacridium_aegyptium_-_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Frontal view of Egyptian locust (Anacridium aegyptium) showing the compound eyes, tiny ocelli and numerous setae","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnacridium_aegyptium_-_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Two_eastern_Lubber_grasshopers_%28Romalea_microptera%29%2C_mating.jpg/500px-Two_eastern_Lubber_grasshopers_%28Romalea_microptera%29%2C_mating.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Two_eastern_Lubber_grasshopers_%28Romalea_microptera%29%2C_mating.jpg/1280px-Two_eastern_Lubber_grasshopers_%28Romalea_microptera%29%2C_mating.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Two_eastern_Lubber_grasshopers_%28Ro